("v567", "entry", "v572")
("v572", "type", "Entry")
("v572", "key", "beforeText")
("v573", "type", "String")
("v573", "scalar", "Claimipedia, opening soon, does it differently. A claim gets a permanent address. Groups judge it with review methods they write down: which evidence counts, how much it weighs, how many independent sources are enough. Each method runs the same way every time. You don’t get one verdict. You see what each method concludes, and exactly where they part ways.")
("v572", "value", "v573")
("v567", "entry", "v574")
("v574", "type", "Entry")
("v574", "key", "html")
("v575", "type", "String")
("v575", "scalar", "<strong>Claimipedia</strong> keeps claims, evidence and review methods distinct. A claim has a stable identity and version. A method states which evidence counts, how it is weighed and what is enough to decide. The working microsite illustrates how the same evidence can produce different conclusions, with the reasons visible.")
("v574", "value", "v575")
